>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `CLARSIMP_TAC`

``` hol4
clasimpLib.CLARSIMP_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Combines safe simplification with non-branching classical reasoning.

`CLARSIMP_TAC thms` first performs safe, assumption-aware full
simplification with the current clasimpset. It then repeatedly clarifies
each residual goal, with safe simplification available as a safe wrapper.
The tactic can succeed with residual goals, but only when the goal state
changes.

Clarification normally avoids branching. Nevertheless, a premise splitter
in the simpset can split a subgoal during simplification. The standard
clasimpset contains `simpLib.split_ss`, so `CLARSIMP_TAC` does not promise
to preserve a single subgoal.

Unmarked theorems are inserted as assumptions. Explicit classical markers,
`Simp`, `Iff`, and generic simplifier controls configure only this call.

### Failure

Fails if simplification and clarification together leave the goal
unchanged. Malformed marked rules can also fail during argument processing.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem clarsimp_tac_example:
  p /\ q ==> p
Proof
  clasimpLib.CLARSIMP_TAC []
QED
```

